{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"31d2b8ebf1f69ba4ac66cb0b4080ed41f0ed5f232b522f159a0a11c2a0b67620","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot git snapshot fetch","key_entities":["src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py","http.lowSpeedLimit","http.lowSpeedTime","_fetch_origin","src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py","_GIT_TIMEOUT","resolve_ref"],"problem_keywords":["git fetch stall","timeout","throughput abort","low-speed detection","review-bot","retry logic"],"propositions":["A git fetch that accepts a connection but sends zero bytes currently stalls for the full 300s wall-clock timeout instead of aborting on throughput starvation within seconds.","The fix adds http.lowSpeedLimit and http.lowSpeedTime config to git fetch operations to abort stalled connections based on throughput floor (default 1000 B/s over 10s window), not wall time.","Low-speed abort failures are retried in-process a bounded number of times to self-heal transient stalls within a single review, while non-throughput failures (auth, bad ref) are not retried.","The git fetch plumbing (lock management, subprocess execution, error classification) is extracted from repo_snapshot.py into a new git_fetch.py module to satisfy the 800 LOC module-size cap."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787328178573894001,"uuid":"25a9ce18-f737-4387-bc94-1a710e8bac30"}